# claude-context index rules for Propria. Byline: Claude Code · Opus 5.5 · 2026-09-26
#
# Propria is one project and is indexed as one codebase (owner 2026-09-26 17:44: "Everything under
# Propria is one repo ... Anything under this repo needs to be indexed together."). The claude-context
# fork (E:/AI_Workspace/Projects/claude-context) applies every .gitignore to its own repository, so a
# nested repository stays in the index under its own rules. These index-only rules apply everywhere,
# nested repositories included, after the .gitignore rules.

# The root .gitignore leaves out the module folders only because they keep their own git histories
# for now (modules/Probata is a folder holding the Probata repository, not a repository itself).
!/modules/Consignatio/
!/modules/Probata/
!/modules/Legal-desktop/
!/modules/vestigia-geodata_processor/
# Consignatio's .gitignore leaves out this folder because it holds two child repositories (the Xplorer
# fork and the build kit); the root .gitignore lists design-contract/ although its files are tracked.
!/modules/Consignatio/Intake/xplorer-copilot-buildkit/
!/design-contract/

# Third-party dependency copies (Go modules in Probata's engine, vendored web assets).
vendor/

# Quarantine folders awaiting the owner's delete, in every repository.
to_be_deleted/

# Tool forks are separate repositories outside Propria (owner 2026-09-26 17:44). The memsearch fork
# clone still sits here while another session works in it; delete this line once it moves to
# E:/AI_Workspace/Projects/memsearch.
/modules/memsearch/
